steps.text:
A time trial (TT) is the test closest to racing, and among the most repeatable (*Noise, worthwhile changes and non-responders*). Field TTs can be short. In 8 trained male cyclists, both 4-min and 20-min TTs repeated well, the 20-min one to within 4.6 W, and 20-min power accounted for 92% of the differences in 60-min power between riders [[c:short-tt]].

For runners the same idea is a 3 km or 5 km TT on a track; for triathletes, a TT in each sport, on separate days.

What turns a hard ride into a test:

- the same course, warm-up and time of day;
- even pacing, rehearsed in a practice trial;
- no drafting, and similar weather.
